{
 "sheet": 1,
 "name": "A1101LLHLT-T",
 "kind": "sensor",
 "manufacturer": "Allegro MicroSystems",
 "title": "A1101, A1102, A1103, A1104, A1106: continuous-time unipolar Hall-effect switches",
 "source": {
  "document": "A1101-DS",
  "revision": "Rev. 18, June 2, 2021",
  "pages": 13
 },
 "summary": "A family of five unipolar Hall-effect switches with an open-drain NMOS output that pulls low when a south-pole field exceeds the operate point and lets go when it falls below the release point. They run from 3.8 to 24 V through an internal regulator, survive ±30 V on the supply, are valid within 4 µs of power-on and need no supply capacitor. The devices differ only in switch points (A1101: BOP 100 G typ, A1102: 180 G, A1103: 280 G, A1104: 35 to 450 G, A1106: 340 G). The A1101LLHLT-T is the A1101 in the 3-pin SOT23W for –40 to 150 °C on a 3000-piece reel.",
