   "id": "pull-up-output",
   "title": "Switch with a pull-up on the output",
   "page": 7,
   "description": "The sensor runs straight from the supply VS on its VCC pin with GND to ground. One load resistor RL ties the open-drain VOUT up to VS, and the output is taken at VOUT: it is high with no field, drops to VOUT(SAT) when a south field passes BOP, and returns high once the field falls under BRP. The part needs no supply capacitor.",
